.so fork.tmac
.PP
.pt_jd_serialize
.RS 4
.PP
This function provides an easy alternative to a custom-developed
print routine.
.B jd_serialize
prints in one of two modes, either fully expanded with each value
on its own line, or fully minimized, having removed all extra spaces
between values and elements.
.TP
.I fd
the file descriptor to which the output will be directed.  An example
would be
.BR STDOUT_FILENO .
.TP
.I node
The node from which the print will be conducted.  The specified node
and all its children will be included in the output.
.TP
.I indent
specifies the indent level to start.
.I indent
values >=0 will print in pretty-mode.
If the value is less than
0, the output will be minimized.
.RE
